TypeScript is a strongly typed superset of JavaScript developed by Microsoft. It compiles to plain JavaScript.

Benefits over JavaScript:
- **Static types** — catch errors at compile time, not runtime
- **Better tooling** — autocomplete, refactoring, go-to-definition
- **Interfaces and generics** — express complex contracts
- **Decorators** — metadata-driven programming

```typescript
// hello.ts
const greeting: string = "Hello, World!";
console.log(greeting);

function greet(name: string): string {
    return `Hello, ${name}!`;
}
console.log(greet("TypeScript"));
```

